      "statement": "PRSP-HMS-3.4, which Victor Petrov approves, defines a seven-state hold lifecycle (OPEN, IN_REVIEW, ESCALATED, RELEASED, REJECTED, BLOCKED, EXPIRED), a twelve-code hold reason (HRC) taxonomy with POL-FCC-014 disclosure tiers (P/C/G/R), data-handling rules for the Restricted description/analystNotes fields and the legacy HMS-to-PPH v1 holdReasonDesc sync (open risk FCT-2004), and interface/control rules including CTRL-PAY-012 maker-checker and CTRL-PAY-031 HRC-01-only digital attestation.",
